            <ArticleTitle>Learned Helplessness in the Rat: An Elusive Phenomenon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/00221309.1982.9709909</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of three experiments, using 48 albino rats as Ss, manipulated the intensity and duration of inescapable treatment shock. Subsequent testing on the acquisition of an FR-3 lever-press response to terminate test shock showed no interference effects whether test shock was the same, less intense, or more intense than treatment shock.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
